---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import Glossary from "../../components/Glossary.astro";
import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../styles/extended.css";
import HistoryTimeline from "../../components/HistoryTimeline.astro";
import history from "../../data/history.json";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/asbe/asbe03.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.description}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
  bannerNotice={metadata.bannerNotice}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "Scope — Held for Rental or Capital Appreciation" },
        { id: "s3", label: "Land Use Rights as Investment Property" },
        { id: "s4", label: "Initial Measurement — At Cost" },
        { id: "s5", label: "THE KEY DIVERGENCE — the Fair Value Model Is Tightly Restricted" },
        { id: "s6", label: "The Cost Model — the Practical Default" },
        { id: "s7", label: "Why China Restricts the Fair Value Model" },
        { id: "s8", label: "Worked Example — Applying the Cost Model" },
        { id: "s9", label: "Worked Example — Qualifying for the Fair Value Model" },
        { id: "s10", label: "Disclosure Requirements" },
        { id: "s11", label: "Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates" },
        { id: "s12", label: "Relationship to IAS 40" },
        { id: "s13", label: "Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s14", label: "Related Standards" },
        { id: "s15", label: "Glossary" }
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>
  <div class="wrap">



<div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Property held for rental income or appreciation, not owner use</div><div class="principle">ASBE No. 3 governs PROPERTY (land or buildings, or BOTH) held to EARN rental income, for CAPITAL appreciation, or BOTH — RATHER than for use in the PRODUCTION or supply of GOODS/services, for administrative PURPOSES, or for SALE in the ordinary course of business. WHILE broadly PARALLELING IAS 40's OWN scope internationally, this Standard TAKES a genuinely MORE RESTRICTIVE approach to WHEN the fair value MEASUREMENT model may be applied (Section 5).</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope — Held for Rental or Capital Appreciation</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">A narrower category than property generally</div><div class="principle">This Standard applies ONLY to property meeting the SPECIFIC "investment property" definition — LEASED-OUT buildings, LEASED-OUT land use rights, and LAND use rights held for CAPITAL appreciation — EXCLUDING owner-occupied property (governed by ASBE No. 4, Fixed Assets) and property HELD for sale in the ORDINARY course of business (governed by ASBE No. 1, Inventories).</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Land Use Rights as Investment Property</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">A reflection of China's state land-ownership system</div><div class="text-supporting">GIVEN that ALL land in China is ULTIMATELY owned by the STATE (or, in RURAL areas, by COLLECTIVES), enterprises HOLD "LAND USE RIGHTS" RATHER than freehold OWNERSHIP — WHERE such rights are HELD for LEASING out or CAPITAL appreciation PURPOSES, they FALL within THIS Standard's scope, DISTINCT from HOW land use rights held for the enterprise's OWN operational USE are classified as INTANGIBLE assets under ASBE No. 6.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>Initial Measurement — At Cost</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Purchase price plus directly attributable costs</div><div class="text-supporting">Investment property is INITIALLY measured at COST — the PURCHASE price, PLUS directly ATTRIBUTABLE expenditure (e.g. professional FEES, property TRANSFER taxes) — CONSISTENT with the GENERAL cost-based initial measurement APPROACH applied throughout the ASBE asset standards.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>THE KEY DIVERGENCE — the Fair Value Model Is Tightly Restricted</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">A genuinely narrower fair value election than IAS 40 permits</div><div class="text-supporting">UNLIKE IAS 40, which permits an entity to FREELY ELECT the fair value MODEL for ALL its investment property (applied CONSISTENTLY across its ENTIRE investment property portfolio), ASBE No. 3 permits the FAIR VALUE model ONLY where there is CLEAR evidence that an ACTIVE, LIQUID property market EXISTS in the SAME (or a COMPARABLE) location, PROVIDING reliable, OBSERVABLE market PRICES sufficient to MEASURE fair value with CONFIDENCE. WHERE this CONDITION is NOT met — which, in PRACTICE, is the SITUATION for MOST Chinese enterprises, given the STILL-DEVELOPING state of many LOCAL property valuation MARKETS — the COST model is REQUIRED instead. This is a genuinely SIGNIFICANT, WELL-KNOWN measurement divergence from IAS 40.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>The Cost Model — the Practical Default</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Depreciation and impairment, much like owner-occupied property</div><div class="text-supporting">UNDER the COST model, investment property is CARRIED at cost LESS accumulated DEPRECIATION (or amortisation, for LAND use rights) and any ACCUMULATED impairment losses — MEASURED in SUBSTANTIALLY the SAME manner as OWNER-OCCUPIED fixed assets under ASBE No. 4, WITH impairment assessed under ASBE No. 8's NO-REVERSAL framework.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Why China Restricts the Fair Value Model</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Caution around unreliable fair value estimates in developing markets</div><div class="text-supporting">The POLICY rationale UNDERLYING this RESTRICTION reflects a BROADER, RECURRING theme ACROSS several ASBE asset STANDARDS (also seen in FIXED assets and BIOLOGICAL assets — see the COMPANION posters): a GENERAL caution around PERMITTING fair value MEASUREMENT where reliable, OBSERVABLE market EVIDENCE may NOT genuinely EXIST across China's DIVERSE and UNEVENLY developed regional PROPERTY and asset MARKETS — PRIORITISING the VERIFIABILITY and OBJECTIVITY of historical COST over the POTENTIAL relevance of fair VALUE information.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Worked Example — Applying the Cost Model</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Depreciating a rental property over its useful life</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: A leased-out office building</div><div class="wk-body">A company holds an office building, leased out to a third-party tenant, with a cost of RMB 80,000,000 and an estimated useful life of 40 years, no active market evidence available for a reliable fair value.</div><div class="wk-answer">The company applies the COST MODEL, recognising annual depreciation of RMB 80,000,000 ÷ 40 = <strong>RMB 2,000,000</strong> — carrying the property at cost LESS accumulated depreciation, CONSISTENT with the treatment of an OWNER-OCCUPIED building under ASBE No. 4.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Worked Example — Qualifying for the Fair Value Model</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">A rare case where an active market genuinely exists</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: A property in a major, highly liquid city market</div><div class="wk-body">A company holds an investment property in a major city with an unusually active, transparent, and liquid commercial property market, providing frequent, reliable comparable transaction data.</div><div class="wk-answer">GIVEN the CLEAR evidence of an ACTIVE market, the company may ELECT the FAIR VALUE model for this PROPERTY — measuring it at FAIR VALUE each period, WITH changes recognised DIRECTLY in the INCOME STATEMENT, WITHOUT depreciation — though this remains the LESS common outcome in PRACTICE across the BROADER ASBE preparer base.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What ASBE No. 3 requires</div><div class="check-list"><span>Measurement model applied (cost or fair value), and the basis for that election</span><span>Depreciation/amortisation method and useful life, where the cost model applies</span><span>Fair value of investment property, disclosed in the notes even where the cost model is used</span></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div>
<div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Whether sufficiently reliable active-market evidence exists to justify the fair value model</span><span>Classifying a property as investment property versus owner-occupied or inventory</span></div></div>
<div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Useful life and depreciation method under the cost model</span><span>Fair value disclosed in the notes, even when not used for measurement</span></div></div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Relationship to IAS 40</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — ASBE 3 vs IAS 40</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Feature</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-warning);">ASBE 3</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-info);">IAS 40</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Fair value model availability</span><span>RESTRICTED — requires clear active-market evidence</span><span>FREE policy choice, applied consistently across the portfolio</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Cost model</span><span>The practical default in most cases</span><span>Available, but genuinely less commonly elected internationally</span></div>
</div>
<div class="note">A GENUINELY significant divergence — in PRACTICE, the VAST majority of Chinese investment property is carried at COST, WHEREAS the fair value model is MORE widely used internationally WHERE IAS 40 applies.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Where every investment property event lands</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Depreciation (cost model)</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span> <span class="badge bp">IS</span></span><span>Recognised as an expense each period</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Fair value change (fair value model, if elected)</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span> <span class="badge bp">IS</span></span><span>Recognised directly in profit or loss</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Standard</span><span>Connection</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>ASBE No. 4</span><span>Fixed Assets — supplies the depreciation and cost-model mechanics this Standard mirrors</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>ASBE No. 6</span><span>Intangible Assets — governs land use rights held for the enterprise's own operational use, outside this Standard's scope</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s15"><span class="num">15</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2">
<div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Investment property</div><div class="glossary-def">Property held to earn rental income, for capital appreciation, or both, rather than for owner use or sale in the ordinary course of business.</div></div>
<div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;"><div class="glossary-term">Land use rights (土地使用权)</div><div class="glossary-def">The right to use state- or collectively-owned land for a defined period, held by enterprises in place of freehold land ownership.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="legend"><div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (Chinese GAAP / ASBE terminology)</div><div class="lrow"><div class="litem"><span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet (资产负债表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bp">IS</span> Income Statement (利润表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge be">SCOE</span> Statement of Changes in Owners' Equity (所有者权益变动表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bc">CFS</span> Cash Flow Statement (现金流量表)</div></div></div>


</div>
  <section id="history">
    <HistoryTimeline items={history.asbe03 || []} />
  </section>
</StandardPageLayout>
